name 'building-data-driven-systems-postassessment-q14_2025'

question 'A developer uses the following pipeline: `data.filter(isAvailable).sort(byPrice).map(renderCard)`. What happens if no items are "available"?'

wrong 'The app will crash during the `.sort()` step.'
wrong 'The `.map()` function will generate error messages on the screen.'
right 'The filter returns an empty array, and the subsequent sort and map operations simply do nothing, resulting in an empty display.'
wrong 'The AI will automatically add more items so the pipeline can finish.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 10

Chaining is "fail-safe" in this regard; if an early step (like filtering) returns an empty list, the later steps (sorting and mapping) just process that empty list, resulting in no items rendered.
MARKDOWN
